{% import 'landing/sections/_shot.html.twig' as shot %}

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════ DRESSING ROOM ═══════════════════════════════ -->
<section id="dressing-room">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-label">Dressing Room Dynamics</div>
        <h2 class="section-title">Your squad has opinions about each other.</h2>
        <p class="section-sub">
            Every player carries a live relationship with every team-mate. Bonds form
            between players who train, room and win together; friction builds between
            the ones who don't. The network is visible, and it moves.
        </p>

        <div class="feature-split">
            <div class="point-list">
                <div class="point">
                    <span class="point-title is-mint">Bonded</span>
                    <p>Solid green links. Bonded players lift each other's morale week on week and hold their form through a bad run.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="point">
                    <span class="point-title is-red">Friction</span>
                    <p>Dashed red links. Friction drags morale down, and a dressing room carrying enough of it will turn on a manager.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="point">
                    <span class="point-title is-plain">Unformed</span>
                    <p>Most of the squad, most of the time. Relationships are earned rather than assigned at signing — a new arrival starts connected to nobody.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="point">
                    <span class="point-title">It compounds</span>
                    <p>Sell the wrong player and you cut three bonds at once. The squad you build is a network, not a list.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <figure class="feature-shot">
                {{ shot.img('dressing-room-network', 'Dressing room overview — squad rated SETTLED, 24% bonded, 76% unformed, 0% friction, average morale 99, with a relationship network mapping links between eleven named players', false, 340) }}
                <figcaption>Key relationship network — tap a face for scores</figcaption>
            </figure>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<hr class="divider">
